1
00:00:02,168 --> 00:00:03,794
NARRATOR:
<i>Previously</i> on The Big Bang Theory:

2
00:00:03,961 --> 00:00:07,589
ALL: We now pronounce you
husband and wife.

3
00:00:07,757 --> 00:00:08,799
[CHEERING]

4
00:00:10,051 --> 00:00:13,512
-I love this part!
-Me too!

5
00:00:13,679 --> 00:00:16,890
I have strongly mixed feelings.

6
00:00:19,018 --> 00:00:22,187
So Howard's really in space?

7
00:00:22,355 --> 00:00:25,858
The International Space Station,
250 miles that way. Heh.

8
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:28,819
Right now Howard
is staring down at our planet...

9
00:00:28,986 --> 00:00:31,488
...like a tiny Jewish Greek god.

10
00:00:32,865 --> 00:00:35,200
Zeus-owitz.

11
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:39,038
I must admit,
I can't help but feel a twinge of envy.

12
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:41,040
He can look out the window...

13
00:00:41,207 --> 00:00:44,960
...and see the majesty of the universe
unfolding before his eyes.

14
00:00:45,127 --> 00:00:48,380
His dim, uncomprehending eyes.

15
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:54,553
It's like a cat in an airport carrying case.

16
00:00:56,347 --> 00:00:58,557
You know,
it's not exactly glamorous up there.

17
00:00:58,724 --> 00:01:02,144
The water the astronauts drink
is made from each other's recycled urine.

18
00:01:03,187 --> 00:01:05,397
Must be nice.

19
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:07,775
Nobody wants anything
that comes out of me.

20
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:18,490
-I wonder what he's doing this very second.
-Conducting experiments in zero gravity.

21
00:01:18,744 --> 00:01:21,371
Peering through his telescope
at the birth of the cosmos.

22
00:01:21,539 --> 00:01:24,416
Whatever it is,
we know his life will never be the same.

23
00:01:24,875 --> 00:01:28,420
MRS. WOLOWITZ [OVER SPEAKER]:
<i>Howard,</i> can you <i>hear</i> me?

24
00:01:28,796 --> 00:01:31,590
I can hear you without the phone!

25
00:01:32,592 --> 00:01:36,554
<i>Don ’t be snippy.</i>
<i>I'm just excited to talk to my baby.</i>

26
00:01:36,721 --> 00:01:39,056
I'm excited to talk to you too.

27
00:01:39,223 --> 00:01:43,723
<i>So, What's this mishegas about you</i>
<i>moving out to go live with the little Polish girl?</i>

28
00:01:45,104 --> 00:01:47,856
How about calling her my wife? Heh.

29
00:01:48,107 --> 00:01:50,442
<i>Wives don ’t take boys from their mothers.</i>

30
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:53,195
They do, that's why we marry them.

31
00:01:55,364 --> 00:01:59,201
<i>I just hope I'm not dead</i>
<i>from a broken heart before you get back.</i>

32
00:01:59,535 --> 00:02:03,872
Ma, please, everyone from NASA
is listening to this phone call.

33
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:07,626
<i>Good, they should know</i>
<i>what a horrible son you are.</i>

34
00:02:07,835 --> 00:02:11,046
Okay, Ma, great talking to you.
Gotta go.

35
00:02:11,505 --> 00:02:12,756
[SIGHS]

36
00:02:12,923 --> 00:02:14,090
Well...

37
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:15,801
...space is ruined.

38
00:02:49,669 --> 00:02:51,504
AMY:
This is so exciting.

39
00:02:52,838 --> 00:02:56,675
Soon my upper lip will be the same
fake-blond as my beautiful best friend.

40
00:02:58,135 --> 00:02:59,928
Hey, this is my natural hair color.

41
00:03:02,515 --> 00:03:04,016
Now.

42
00:03:04,850 --> 00:03:08,395
So does Sheldon have anything special
planned for you tomorrow night?

43
00:03:08,562 --> 00:03:13,024
Yes. According to the relationship agreement,
on the anniversary of our first date...

44
00:03:13,192 --> 00:03:16,028
...he must take me to a nice dinner,
ask about my day...

45
00:03:16,195 --> 00:03:18,197
...and engage in casual physical contact...

46
00:03:18,364 --> 00:03:21,492
...that a disinterested onlooker
might mistake for intimacy.

47
00:03:22,201 --> 00:03:23,243
That's hot.

48
00:03:24,829 --> 00:03:27,039
You kids better use protection.

49
00:03:28,374 --> 00:03:30,751
-How long does this stay on?
-Just a couple minutes.

50
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:34,630
-You've really never done this before?
-Once in high school. But I dozed off...

51
00:03:34,797 --> 00:03:37,674
...and woke up with second degree
chemical burns on my face.

52
00:03:38,342 --> 00:03:41,345
Oh, my gosh, that's awful.
Did the other kids make fun of you?

53
00:03:41,512 --> 00:03:44,389
No, I had a cover story.
I told everyone it was herpes.

54
00:03:46,225 --> 00:03:50,395
-So how's everything with you and Leonard?
-I don't know. It's still kind of weird.

55
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:54,024
We haven't really recovered
since he proposed to me in the middle of sex.

56
00:03:54,191 --> 00:03:56,443
Oh. Boo-hoo.

57
00:03:57,027 --> 00:03:58,862
If Sheldon proposed to me during sex...

58
00:03:59,029 --> 00:04:01,740
...my ovaries would grab onto him
and never let go.

59
00:04:07,913 --> 00:04:11,291
Leonard, where do you stand
on the anthropic principle?

60
00:04:11,751 --> 00:04:15,755
-Interesting question. On the one hand--
-You don't even know what it is, do you?

61
00:04:16,756 --> 00:04:18,883
The anthropic principle states...

62
00:04:19,049 --> 00:04:22,969
...that if we wish to explain
why our universe exists the way it does...

63
00:04:23,137 --> 00:04:25,889
...the answer is that
it must have qualities...

64
00:04:26,056 --> 00:04:28,391
...that allow intelligent creatures
to arise...

65
00:04:28,559 --> 00:04:30,561
...who are capable of asking the question.

66
00:04:30,728 --> 00:04:34,064
As I am doing so eloquently right now.

67
00:04:35,024 --> 00:04:37,026
I know what the anthropic principle is.

68
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:39,403
Of course.
I just explained it to you.

69
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:42,948
Now, where do you stand on it?

70
00:04:43,115 --> 00:04:45,117
-Where do you stand on it?
-Strong|y pro.

71
00:04:45,284 --> 00:04:47,953
Then I believe that God
created the world in six days...

72
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:50,413
...and on the seventh
he made you to annoy me.

73
00:04:54,919 --> 00:04:56,128
-Hey, guys.
-Hey.

74
00:04:56,295 --> 00:04:59,506
Raj, where do you stand
on the anthropic principle?

75
00:04:59,673 --> 00:05:01,591
-I'm all for it.
-Thattaboy.

76
00:05:01,759 --> 00:05:04,636
Why do you believe that he knows
what it is, and I don't?

77
00:05:04,804 --> 00:05:06,263
Oh, Leonard...

78
00:05:06,430 --> 00:05:09,975
...let's not take a saw to the branch
we're sitting on, shall we?

79
00:05:10,810 --> 00:05:13,687
Hey, if you guys are free tonight
I heard about a spa...

80
00:05:13,854 --> 00:05:16,314
...where you soak your feet
in a pool of fish...

81
00:05:16,482 --> 00:05:18,192
...that eat the dead skin off them.

82
00:05:19,777 --> 00:05:21,820
I don't need to tell you, in Los Angeles...

83
00:05:21,987 --> 00:05:23,989
...sand a| season is year round.

84
00:05:25,366 --> 00:05:28,160
-Actually, I'm hanging out with Penny.
-Oh, okay.

85
00:05:28,327 --> 00:05:29,953
Sounds like it's me and you.

86
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:32,497
How about we sic some guppies
on those puppies?

87
00:05:33,958 --> 00:05:36,460
As I've stated before
on numerous occasions...

88
00:05:36,627 --> 00:05:39,379
...the only sea creature
I would consider being eaten by...

89
00:05:39,588 --> 00:05:43,633
...is the Kraken. Because the last words
I would hear are "release the Kraken."

90
00:05:44,885 --> 00:05:46,678
That never gets old.

91
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:48,430
[IN DEEP VOICE]
Release the Kraken!

92
00:05:48,597 --> 00:05:50,140
[IN NORMAL VOICE]
Oh, chills.

93
00:05:50,307 --> 00:05:52,976
Besides, I'm having dinner with Amy.

94
00:05:53,352 --> 00:05:55,896
Oh, okay. I'll just go home and be alone.

95
00:05:56,105 --> 00:06:00,484
Which is cool.
I eat alone, I sleep alone, I cry alone, so...

96
00:06:01,318 --> 00:06:02,360
...coo|.

97
00:06:04,697 --> 00:06:05,823
Darn.

98
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:08,826
If you weren't busy I'd ask you to join us.

99
00:06:09,493 --> 00:06:12,204
Really? I can come? Thanks.

100
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:15,499
Sheldon, are you sure you wanna bring Raj
on your date night?

101
00:06:15,666 --> 00:06:17,376
Oh, absolutely.

102
00:06:17,543 --> 00:06:20,003
I have a contractual obligation...

103
00:06:20,170 --> 00:06:23,756
...to provide Amy with conversation
and casual physical contact.

104
00:06:23,924 --> 00:06:28,386
But nowhere is it specified
that I can't outsource that to an Indian.

105
00:06:33,726 --> 00:06:35,227
BERNADETTE [ON MONITOR]:
<i>Howie?</i>

106
00:06:35,769 --> 00:06:39,564
-Howie?
-Hey, there's my beautiful bride.

107
00:06:39,732 --> 00:06:41,942
-Can you see me?
-I <i>can.</i>

108
00:06:42,151 --> 00:06:44,695
<i>-How</i> are <i>you?</i>
-I'm amazing.

109
00:06:44,862 --> 00:06:47,197
This is even better than I dreamed.

110
00:06:47,364 --> 00:06:49,407
I look out the window...

111
00:06:49,575 --> 00:06:52,035
...and it's all so unbelievable.

112
00:06:52,202 --> 00:06:56,702
<i>Good for you. I just had</i> a <i>seemingly</i>
<i>endless dinner with your</i> mom.

113
00:06:58,542 --> 00:07:00,710
Oh, yeah? That's nice. Heh.

114
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:04,923
<i>It was. Until I found out you never told her</i>
<i>we 're not gonna live with her.</i>

115
00:07:05,090 --> 00:07:08,176
<i>Let's talk about that for a minute.</i>

116
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:12,932
Hey, look, this pen is floating. Heh.

117
00:07:13,265 --> 00:07:15,767
How crazy is that?

118
00:07:18,896 --> 00:07:21,231
<i>You said you told her but you never did.</i>

119
00:07:21,398 --> 00:07:24,651
Okay, okay, I know you're upset...

120
00:07:24,818 --> 00:07:28,988
...but let me share something
I've learned since I got here.

121
00:07:29,907 --> 00:07:33,493
You realize how small
your problems are...

122
00:07:33,702 --> 00:07:36,746
...when you're looking down
on them from space.

123
00:07:36,914 --> 00:07:39,708
Heh. Come on,
that's gotta make you feel better.

124
00:07:40,292 --> 00:07:42,794
<i>How clear is the image of me</i>
<i>on that screen?</i>

125
00:07:43,295 --> 00:07:44,421
Pretty clear. Heh.

126
00:07:44,588 --> 00:07:47,132
<i>Do I look like I feel better?</i>

127
00:07:48,258 --> 00:07:51,427
I mean, it's not, like, HD quality.

128
00:07:52,096 --> 00:07:55,432
<i>Listen, you're gonna talk to your mother</i>
<i>and you're gonna fix this.</i>

129
00:07:55,599 --> 00:07:58,518
<i>Or that thing I said I was gonna do to you</i>
<i>when you got home...</i>

130
00:07:58,727 --> 00:08:01,104
<i>you can do to yourself.</i>

131
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:06,484
Like he's been doing since he got here.

132
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:11,615
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS]

133
00:08:11,782 --> 00:08:14,826
Sheldon, this place is so romantic.

134
00:08:14,994 --> 00:08:17,955
Aw.... I'm glad you like it. Raj picked it out.

135
00:08:19,748 --> 00:08:21,875
When you see him,
tell him I say thank you.

136
00:08:22,042 --> 00:08:23,543
Tell him yourself.

137
00:08:24,461 --> 00:08:26,963
Yoo-hoo! Over here.

138
00:08:29,133 --> 00:08:31,510
I don't understand. What's he doing here?

139
00:08:31,677 --> 00:08:34,805
-I invited him.
-On our date?

140
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:36,556
Sheldon, that's not okay.

141
00:08:36,724 --> 00:08:41,145
Oh. Yes, it is. There's a loophole
in the relationship agreement.

142
00:08:41,353 --> 00:08:42,854
You found a loophole?

143
00:08:45,524 --> 00:08:47,859
Sorry I started without you...

144
00:08:48,027 --> 00:08:51,530
...I'm a little nervous.
It's been a long time since I've been on a date.

145
00:08:52,406 --> 00:08:55,367
I can't believe
I bleached my mustache for this.

146
00:08:55,534 --> 00:08:59,162
You should go to my girl,
she'll knock out those sideburns for free.

147
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:10,382
You know, Amy, I don't think
you and I have had a real conversation.

148
00:09:10,549 --> 00:09:13,218
Let's use tonight
to get to know each other better.

149
00:09:14,178 --> 00:09:15,554
You start.

150
00:09:18,682 --> 00:09:19,933
Go home.

151
00:09:21,018 --> 00:09:23,437
-I don't understand.
-Sheldon, how could you do this?

152
00:09:23,604 --> 00:09:26,732
-It's our second anniversary.
-It's your anniversary?

153
00:09:27,441 --> 00:09:29,860
Oh, my God, I had no idea.

154
00:09:30,194 --> 00:09:32,237
Amy, please, let me make this right.

155
00:09:32,821 --> 00:09:34,781
-Thank you.
-My pleasure. Waiter?

156
00:09:34,948 --> 00:09:37,742
A bottle of champagne
and three glasses.

157
00:09:38,702 --> 00:09:41,579
Oh, boy, isn't this romantic?

158
00:09:42,081 --> 00:09:46,085
I hope that's a rhetorical question
because I have no clue.

159
00:09:48,420 --> 00:09:50,588
Mm. This is great, what's the occasion?

160
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:53,967
No occasion.
Things have been a little weird between us...

161
00:09:54,134 --> 00:09:56,719
...so I wanted to throw together
a fun night for you.

162
00:09:56,887 --> 00:09:58,805
-That is so sweet.
-I got your favorites:

163
00:09:58,972 --> 00:10:03,226
Beer, wings, sliders, we can watch
the football game. I even painted my stomach.

164
00:10:06,063 --> 00:10:08,315
-Go sports?
-WeII?

165
00:10:08,482 --> 00:10:11,943
In case you were in the mood for baseball,
I didn't wanna look ridiculous.

166
00:10:12,653 --> 00:10:15,447
-This is awesome, I love it.
-Good, I'm glad.

167
00:10:15,614 --> 00:10:17,949
I worked my ass off,
so this is what I needed.

168
00:10:18,158 --> 00:10:21,161
Great, just relax and enjoy.
Tonight is all about you.

169
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:22,788
Ah. Thank you.

170
00:10:23,205 --> 00:10:24,623
[CHUCKLES]

171
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:26,291
[SIGHS]

172
00:10:26,458 --> 00:10:29,085
So where exactly are we
in this relationship?

173
00:10:30,629 --> 00:10:33,465
Oh, come on, I just told you
I had a hard day.

174
00:10:33,632 --> 00:10:36,635
-You're right, I'm sorry. Let's watch the game.
-Great.

175
00:10:37,052 --> 00:10:38,803
[SIGHS]

176
00:10:38,971 --> 00:10:42,683
Just know, the longer we wait
to talk about it the weirder it gets.

177
00:10:43,475 --> 00:10:46,603
Sweetie, can I just be the girl tonight?

178
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:49,147
Absolutely. You're the girl, I'm the guy.

179
00:10:49,773 --> 00:10:52,317
Watch your football game
while I make you a plate here.

180
00:10:52,484 --> 00:10:53,943
Thank you.

181
00:10:54,945 --> 00:10:56,279
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

182
00:10:56,446 --> 00:10:59,282
I'll get it. Go sports! Heh.

183
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:03,287
Hello-Io-Io.

184
00:11:04,204 --> 00:11:06,372
I thought you were out
with Sheldon and Amy.

185
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:09,960
I was, but it's their anniversary,
and I didn't wanna be a third wheel...

186
00:11:10,127 --> 00:11:13,004
...so I figured I'd hang out
with you and Penny on your date.

187
00:11:13,839 --> 00:11:17,467
It's not really a great time.
Penny and I have some things to talk about.

188
00:11:17,634 --> 00:11:19,052
PENNY:
No we don't, come on in!

189
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:21,805
Sweet.

190
00:11:22,139 --> 00:11:25,058
I can't believe
I shaved my stomach for this.

191
00:11:30,731 --> 00:11:32,691
DIMITRI:
Hey, Froot Loops.

192
00:11:36,361 --> 00:11:38,029
You got a phone call.

193
00:11:38,447 --> 00:11:39,739
Who is it?

194
00:11:39,948 --> 00:11:43,868
A woman who says she's your mother
but sounds like your father.

195
00:11:47,039 --> 00:11:48,081
[TURNS SPEAKER ON]

196
00:11:48,248 --> 00:11:49,540
Hey, Ma.

197
00:11:49,708 --> 00:11:53,503
You know, we could see each other
if you turn on the computer.

198
00:11:53,670 --> 00:11:55,755
MRS. WOLOWITZ:
<i>I'm not going near that</i> fakakta <i>thing.</i>

199
00:11:55,964 --> 00:11:58,466
<i>I'll catch a computer virus!</i>

200
00:11:59,843 --> 00:12:02,887
You can't catch a computer virus.

201
00:12:03,055 --> 00:12:07,184
<i>Oh, so now you’re an astronaut</i>
<i>and a doctor?</i>

202
00:12:08,352 --> 00:12:09,978
What do you want, Ma?

203
00:12:11,230 --> 00:12:14,983
<i>Your Wife says you have</i>
<i>something important to tell me.</i>

204
00:12:15,692 --> 00:12:18,569
Okay, here it is:

205
00:12:19,029 --> 00:12:23,074
Bernadette and I
are starting a life together.

206
00:12:23,242 --> 00:12:24,368
-And--
<i>-Oh, God.</i>

207
00:12:24,534 --> 00:12:26,202
<i>You are gonna leave me!</i>

208
00:12:26,370 --> 00:12:28,413
_Ma__
<i>-It's okay.</i>

209
00:12:28,705 --> 00:12:30,873
<i>Your father left me, you left me.</i>

210
00:12:31,041 --> 00:12:34,919
<i>I guess I'm just the kind of person</i>
<i>people like to leave.</i>

211
00:12:37,214 --> 00:12:41,134
It's not definite. I'll talk to Bernadette.

212
00:12:41,301 --> 00:12:42,385
<i>Don ’t bother.</i>

213
00:12:42,552 --> 00:12:47,052
<i>I'll just go sit in</i> a <i>hole in the ground</i>
<i>so I’m no trouble when I die.</i>

214
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:50,226
Stop it, Ma.

215
00:12:50,394 --> 00:12:53,605
I'm sure I can get Bernie to come around.

216
00:12:53,772 --> 00:12:57,275
<i>I knew it! I knew she was behind this.</i>

217
00:12:57,442 --> 00:13:01,942
<i>You listen to me, if you wanna be a man</i>
<i>you can't let a woman tell you What to do.</i>

218
00:13:04,658 --> 00:13:06,451
Okay, okay.

219
00:13:06,618 --> 00:13:10,455
I can't believe these people
won the Cold War.

220
00:13:12,582 --> 00:13:15,418
Now, can we please change the subject?

221
00:13:15,585 --> 00:13:20,085
<i>Fine. Explain Why you've been gone so long</i>
<i>and I haven't gotten a single letter.</i>

222
00:13:20,632 --> 00:13:23,426
<i>Not even</i> a <i>lousy postcard!</i>

223
00:13:25,804 --> 00:13:27,806
[ANNOUNCER SPEAKING
INDISTINCTLY ON TV]

224
00:13:28,807 --> 00:13:31,643
You know,
I'm growing to like American football.

225
00:13:31,810 --> 00:13:33,686
-Yeah, it's fun, isn't it?
-WeII...

226
00:13:33,854 --> 00:13:38,354
...it's not the balls-to-the-wall action
of badminton or cricket, but hey...

227
00:13:39,192 --> 00:13:40,693
...what is?

228
00:13:42,154 --> 00:13:43,655
Who's ready for another beer?

229
00:13:43,822 --> 00:13:45,073
-I'm good.
-No, thank you.

230
00:13:45,615 --> 00:13:46,991
Girls.

231
00:13:48,118 --> 00:13:50,829
I am having the nicest time.

232
00:13:50,996 --> 00:13:53,623
You guys are like family to me.
You know that, right?

233
00:13:53,790 --> 00:13:55,500
That's great. Get out.

234
00:13:56,335 --> 00:13:59,838
-What? Why?
-Penny and I have some issues to talk about.

235
00:14:00,005 --> 00:14:02,966
Oh, pish on your issues.

236
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:05,510
You guys are fine.

237
00:14:05,802 --> 00:14:08,221
Yes, you've had some bumps
along the way.

238
00:14:08,388 --> 00:14:11,724
I mean, Penny, you've always known
how this man has felt about you.

239
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:14,185
But you made him grovel for affection.

240
00:14:14,353 --> 00:14:16,646
-Okay, hold on--
-Don't blame yourself.

241
00:14:16,813 --> 00:14:18,689
He was a groveler from way back.

242
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:24,153
But the point is,
the two of you got past it.

243
00:14:24,363 --> 00:14:28,200
And you go and propose to this poor girl
in the middle of sex?

244
00:14:28,367 --> 00:14:30,369
That was some weak tea, dude.

245
00:14:31,870 --> 00:14:33,830
Some people might say it was romantic.

246
00:14:34,247 --> 00:14:35,539
Yeah, no.

247
00:14:36,917 --> 00:14:39,878
But yet, here you two are still together.

248
00:14:40,545 --> 00:14:43,005
Even after you and I
had our crazy naked night.

249
00:14:43,173 --> 00:14:44,549
PENNY: That's enough.
LEONARD: Okay.

250
00:14:44,716 --> 00:14:45,883
I'm just saying...

251
00:14:46,051 --> 00:14:48,011
...that after all you've been through...

252
00:14:48,178 --> 00:14:52,348
...you get to look into each other's eyes
and say I love you.

253
00:14:52,766 --> 00:14:54,225
And that's beautiful.

254
00:14:57,729 --> 00:15:00,231
Actually, to this day
she's never really said it.

255
00:15:01,566 --> 00:15:03,734
Oh, Penny, that's ridiculous!

256
00:15:04,945 --> 00:15:07,530
You know you love him.
Look him in the eyes and say it.

257
00:15:07,697 --> 00:15:10,366
-Raj.
-You know you want to say it. Say it.

258
00:15:11,243 --> 00:15:13,245
Say you love him.

259
00:15:15,247 --> 00:15:16,706
Say it!

260
00:15:22,045 --> 00:15:23,796
I really thought she would say it.

261
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:35,058
Have I ever told you
you're like a sexy praying mantis?

262
00:15:37,477 --> 00:15:39,937
Every time you drink alcohol.

263
00:15:40,772 --> 00:15:43,483
You know, what's wonderful
about the praying mantis...

264
00:15:44,067 --> 00:15:46,444
...they devour their mate.

265
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:48,446
Your point being?

266
00:15:55,996 --> 00:15:57,998
Dessert is served.

267
00:15:59,207 --> 00:16:01,584
I just had cobbler.

268
00:16:02,836 --> 00:16:04,420
You know what?

269
00:16:04,921 --> 00:16:06,422
I'm done with this.

270
00:16:07,966 --> 00:16:10,510
-But where are you going?
-I'm leaving.

271
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:13,429
You can't leave, I need you.

272
00:16:16,766 --> 00:16:19,351
-You do?
-Yes.

273
00:16:19,728 --> 00:16:21,438
You're my ride.

274
00:16:23,773 --> 00:16:25,065
Sheldon...

275
00:16:25,233 --> 00:16:28,069
...you either say something meaningful
and from the heart...

276
00:16:28,236 --> 00:16:29,654
...or you and I are done.

277
00:16:31,406 --> 00:16:32,740
All right.

278
00:16:34,701 --> 00:16:36,411
Please.

279
00:16:37,537 --> 00:16:38,746
[SHELDON CLEARS THROAT]

280
00:16:40,207 --> 00:16:41,791
Amy...

281
00:16:43,001 --> 00:16:45,003
...when I look in your eyes...

282
00:16:45,212 --> 00:16:47,505
...and you're looking back in mine...

283
00:16:47,672 --> 00:16:49,423
...everything feels...

284
00:16:49,591 --> 00:16:51,467
...not quite normal...

285
00:16:51,676 --> 00:16:53,511
...because I feel...

286
00:16:53,929 --> 00:16:57,265
...stronger and weaker at the same time.

287
00:16:57,432 --> 00:16:59,934
I feel excited...

288
00:17:00,101 --> 00:17:03,187
...and at the same time, terrified.

289
00:17:04,356 --> 00:17:05,607
The truth is...

290
00:17:05,857 --> 00:17:08,985
...I don't know what I feel...

291
00:17:09,152 --> 00:17:12,280
...except I know what kind of man
I want to be.

292
00:17:14,282 --> 00:17:15,992
Sheldon.

293
00:17:16,535 --> 00:17:17,786
That was beautiful.

294
00:17:17,953 --> 00:17:21,790
I should hope so,
that's from the first <i>Spider-Man</i> movie.

295
00:17:26,461 --> 00:17:28,004
I'll take it.

296
00:17:29,881 --> 00:17:33,384
Good.
Now, I assume we're splitting the check?

297
00:17:37,973 --> 00:17:40,183
-Hey, Stuart.
-Oh, hey.

298
00:17:40,475 --> 00:17:42,143
I was actually just about to close.

299
00:17:42,310 --> 00:17:44,562
-Oh, I'm sorry, I'll leave.
-No, no, it's okay.

300
00:17:44,771 --> 00:17:46,230
-Hang out.
-You sure?

301
00:17:46,398 --> 00:17:48,650
Yeah, you're my first customer today.

302
00:17:49,484 --> 00:17:50,818
All right, great.

303
00:17:50,986 --> 00:17:53,738
I'm, uh, having a nightcap,
you wanna join me?

304
00:17:54,155 --> 00:17:57,491
-What are you drinking?
-Coffee liqueur in a Chewbacca mug.

305
00:17:58,326 --> 00:18:00,411
I call it a sad-tini.

306
00:18:01,329 --> 00:18:03,414
Perfect for the night I'm having,
thank you.

307
00:18:03,623 --> 00:18:08,123
-Mm. Nice not to drink alone.
-Amen to that.

308
00:18:09,087 --> 00:18:12,757
Sometimes I pour a little chardonnay
into my dog's water bowl.

309
00:18:14,342 --> 00:18:16,427
-You're kidding?
-He's kind of a mean drunk...

310
00:18:16,595 --> 00:18:17,846
...but what you gonna do?

311
00:18:18,722 --> 00:18:20,765
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

312
00:18:20,932 --> 00:18:22,516
-A little music?
-Sure.

313
00:18:23,226 --> 00:18:25,228
[BOSSA NOVA PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS]

314
00:18:26,271 --> 00:18:29,774
Mm. Bossa nova.

315
00:18:29,941 --> 00:18:33,319
You listen to that with your hips
as well as your ears.

316
00:18:35,196 --> 00:18:37,031
Ahh.

317
00:18:37,574 --> 00:18:40,910
Something about Latin music...

318
00:18:41,077 --> 00:18:45,577
...makes me feel
like I'm on a white sand beach in Rio.

319
00:18:46,291 --> 00:18:47,458
Yeah?

320
00:18:47,876 --> 00:18:51,796
Sun, the waves, the beautiful bodies...

321
00:18:51,963 --> 00:18:55,049
...tanned and glistening with sweat.

322
00:19:11,149 --> 00:19:13,234
-I should go.
-Yeah.

323
00:19:13,818 --> 00:19:17,571
-Uh, thank you for the drink.
-No problem.

324
00:19:17,864 --> 00:19:18,906
[RAJ SIGHS]

325
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:20,824
-Hey, Stuart.
-Yeah?

326
00:19:21,743 --> 00:19:24,162
You wanna hang out tomorrow night?

327
00:19:24,371 --> 00:19:26,748
Maybe grab a bite to eat
or catch a late movie?

328
00:19:26,915 --> 00:19:30,501
Yeah, I'd like to
but I'm a little tight on funds.

329
00:19:30,794 --> 00:19:33,588
No problem, my treat.
I'll swing by after work.

330
00:19:34,130 --> 00:19:36,423
-Okay.
-Okay.

331
00:19:40,387 --> 00:19:42,472
I could do worse.

332
00:19:48,853 --> 00:19:52,314
BERNADETTE: <i>That’s such good news, Howie.</i>
<i>Thank you for telling her.</i>

333
00:19:52,482 --> 00:19:55,401
Hey, I'm a grown man.
I'm gonna live with my wife.

334
00:19:55,568 --> 00:19:59,738
My mother's just gonna have to learn
to make do on her own.

335
00:20:00,073 --> 00:20:01,574
<i>Was she upset?</i>

336
00:20:01,741 --> 00:20:04,744
Who can tell? She yells everything.

337
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:08,581
She might have been upset.

338
00:20:08,915 --> 00:20:10,499
She might have been hungry.

339
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:15,254
<i>Thanks for fixing it. [love you.</i>

340
00:20:15,463 --> 00:20:18,507
I love you too. Sweet dreams.
I'll talk to you tomorrow.

341
00:20:18,925 --> 00:20:21,427
<i>Goodnight, Rocket Man.</i>

342
00:20:21,761 --> 00:20:25,347
To infinity and beyond, baby.

343
00:20:27,267 --> 00:20:31,767
Loops, you realize you just lied your ass off
to your Wife and your mother.

344
00:20:32,939 --> 00:20:36,192
-I know.
-What are you gonna do when you get back?

345
00:20:36,693 --> 00:20:39,112
Oh, I'm never going back. Heh.

346
00:21:06,931 --> 00:21:08,933
[English - US - SDH]

